 "segments": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "s": 0.35,
   "e": 6.143,
   "text": "Before we look ten years ahead, I want to share a few ideas of my own.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.793,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 6.405,
   "e": 9.581,
   "text": "They are research directions, not results.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.176,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 10.147,
   "e": 12.436,
   "text": "Some of them may be wrong.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.289,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 12.656,
   "e": 16.805,
   "text": "But I think each one is worth someone's PhD.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.149,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 17.884,
   "e": 19.14,
   "text": "The first idea:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.257,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 19.728,
   "e": 23.462,
   "text": "rewire tiles, not synapses.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.734,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 24.045,
   "e": 29.677,
   "text": "Theorem three told us that random sparse graphs starve the GPU.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.632,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 29.98,
   "e": 33.947,
   "text": "But a tensor core does not see synapses.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.967,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 34.567,
   "e": 37.761,
   "text": "It sees small dense tiles.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.194,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 39.011,
   "e": 45.109,
   "text": "So what if structural plasticity worked at exactly that granularity,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 6.097,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 45.404,
   "e": 54.581,
   "text": "growing and pruning whole sixteen-by-sixteen blocks, the way RigL grows and prunes individual weights during training?",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 9.178,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 54.851,
   "e": 58.767,
   "text": "The network still rewires its own topology,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.917,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 59.387,
   "e": 62.997,
   "text": "but every piece that survives stays dense.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.61,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 63.697,
   "e": 74.771,
   "text": "On my laptop, the same ninety percent sparsity ran five and a half times faster as sixteen-by-sixteen tiles than as scattered synapses,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 11.074,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 75.161,
   "e": 77.571,
   "text": "even with a naive implementation.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.409,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 77.977,
   "e": 82.911,
   "text": "A real block-sparse kernel should close much more of the gap.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.934,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 83.631,
   "e": 84.901,
   "text": "The second idea:",
   "dur": 1.27,
   "voiced": 82,
   "sim": 0.71,
   "f0": 113.779,
   "st": -2.039,
   "range_st": 11.704,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 85.063,
   "e": 87.247,
   "text": "spectral homeostasis.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.184,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 87.825,
   "e": 94.087,
   "text": "Theorem one showed that local Hebbian learning collapses toward a single eigenvector.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 6.261,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 94.493,
   "e": 99.041,
   "text": "Real neurons fight a similar runaway with homeostatic plasticity.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.548,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 100.239,
   "e": 106.347,
   "text": "What if the homeostatic target were the shape of the spectrum itself,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 6.108,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 106.58,
   "e": 116.373,
   "text": "so that every layer is gently pushed back whenever its effective rank starts to fall, using only statistics it can measure locally?",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 9.793,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 117.623,
   "e": 121.672,
   "text": "The question I would most like answered is simple:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.048,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 121.916,
   "e": 128.31,
   "text": "can a purely local rule keep many modes alive, the way attention does?",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 6.394,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 129.118,
   "e": 130.239,
   "text": "The third idea:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.121,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "s": 130.507,
   "e": 132.564,
   "text": "let the network sleep.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.057,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "s": 132.882,
   "e": 137.516,
   "text": "Brains separate fast learning from slow consolidation.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.634,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "s": 138.013,
   "e": 140.643,
   "text": "The hippocampus records the day,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.63,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "s": 140.865,
   "e": 144.996,
   "text": "and sleep replays it into the cortex.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.132,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "s": 145.256,
   "e": 147.729,
   "text": "A language model could do the same.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.473,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "s": 148.121,
   "e": 153.466,
   "text": "Fast weights and delta-rule memories, written during every conversation.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.346,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "s": 154.716,
   "e": 162.76,
   "text": "Then, offline, replayed and distilled into the slow weights with ordinary backpropagation.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 8.044,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "s": 163.731,
   "e": 167.498,
   "text": "Plasticity at inference, stability in training.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.766,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 33,
   "s": 167.797,
   "e": 169.776,
   "text": "Two timescales,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.979,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 34,
   "s": 169.896,
   "e": 175.776,
   "text": "and perhaps no catastrophic forgetting, if the replay is chosen well.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.881,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 35,
   "s": 176.476,
   "e": 177.473,
   "text": "And the fourth:",
   "dur": 0.997,
   "voiced": 47,
   "sim": 0.588,
   "f0": 116.218,
   "st": -1.672,
   "range_st": 4.815,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 36,
   "s": 177.748,
   "e": 180.05,
   "text": "three-factor learning for credit.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.302,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 37,
   "s": 180.313,
   "e": 189.149,
   "text": "A method called e-prop showed that eligibility traces stored at each synapse, combined with a single broadcast learning signal,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 8.836,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 38,
   "s": 189.535,
   "e": 194.373,
   "text": "can approximate backpropagation through time in spiking networks.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.837,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 39,
   "s": 194.593,
   "e": 197.055,
   "text": "Pair that with neuromorphic hardware,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.463,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 40,
   "s": 197.645,
   "e": 203.237,
   "text": "and the variance explosion of Theorem three might finally be tamed.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.592,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 41,
   "s": 204.297,
   "e": 208.781,
   "text": "If any of these sparks something for you, run with it.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.484,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 42,
   "s": 209.466,
   "e": 213.013,
   "text": "That is how this field moves forward.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.547,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  }
 ]
